{"id": "EUVD-2026-83285", "enisaUuid": "9ee9baaf-3461-3a7d-8196-c6a55e41442a", "description": "vLLM through 0.29.0 contains a memory corruption vulnerability in the Triton _bincount_kernel where prompt token IDs index the penalty prompt-presence bitset without bounds checking against vocabulary size. Attackers can submit multimodal audio requests with tokens equal to vocabulary size, causing out-of-bounds writes that corrupt concurrent requests' sampler state and alter repetition penalty behavior.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T19:06:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:23:15", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49081", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.29.0/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/penalties.py#L241-L255", "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/v0.29.0/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/penalties.py#L33-L37", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vllm-through-0.29.0-adjacent-request-sampler-state-corruption-via-unvalidated-prompt-token-ids"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q9hm-g73w-q6wp", "CVE-2026-93841", "PYSEC-2026-3999"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cf2efac0-6fde-3baa-8a78-3a44adfd4999", "product": {"name": "vllm", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.29.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1beee48f-a3ce-38f7-8054-c5b9daea6789", "vendor": {"name": "vllm-project"}}], "isExploited": false}